TinyDLT
A lightweight multi-RSU DAG ledger for intelligent transportation systems. ESP32-class vehicles act as thin clients; several independently operated roadside units (RSUs) each keep a full replica of the ledger. A transaction is confirmed only when a quorum of RSUs has validated it and a later transaction has approved it, so no single RSU can confirm anything on its own.
This repository contains the RSU software, the vehicle firmware, the experiment procedure, the analysis scripts and the raw logs behind the paper:
> **tinyDLT: A Lightweight Multi-RSU DAG Ledger with Quorum Confirmation for Intelligent Transportation Systems: Design, Hardware Implementation, and Evaluation** (under review).
